This goal model captures the various decision points and operational steps described in the mission. The fallback (OR) decompositions allow the system to adapt when, for example, the inpatient cannot retrieve food from the tray or when human assistance is unavailable. The sequential (AND) decompositions ensure that critical monitoring (tracking/alerting) and coordination (door opening) steps are performed in order.

